  "lastWords" : "I filled the hole by induction on `m`, and `check_file` reports success on the final file, with no errors and no holes left.\n\n```agda\n+-comm zero n = sym (+-identityʳ n)\n+-comm (suc m) n = trans (cong suc (+-comm m n)) (sym (+-suc n m))\n  where open import Relation.Binary.PropositionalEquality using (trans)\n```\n\n- **Zero case:** `0 + n` reduces to `n`, so the goal is `n ≡ n + 0`. That is the provided `+-identityʳ n`, flipped with `sym`.\n- **Successor case:** the recursive call turns `suc (m + n)` into `suc (n + m)`. The provided `+-suc`, flipped with `sym`, then rewrites that into `n + suc m`.",
